# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots mongod (no --auth) with --fork and then execs
# `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the daemon is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, which is what makes
#     the "enabled auth in config but never restarted mongod" case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting mongod cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART mongod with --auth, not merely
# create a user — the running server is still accepting unauthenticated clients.
